# NVIDIA RTX 3050 6GB Laptop (GA107BM, 10de:25ec); installed only when an NVIDIA GPU is present.
# linux-cachyos-nvidia-open is the open kernel module prebuilt for the linux-cachyos kernel; it is
# versioned with the kernel and with nvidia-utils, so they always update together.
# Installed with these, as their dependencies (checked in the CachyOS package index, 2026-11-12):
#   nvidia-utils       -> egl-wayland (and eglexternalplatform), egl-wayland2, egl-gbm, egl-x11, libglvnd,
#                         and the GPU firmware itself (gsp_ga10x.bin for this card), so linux-firmware-nvidia,
#                         which is for the nouveau and nova drivers, is not needed
#   lib32-nvidia-utils -> the whole 32-bit graphics chain (lib32-libglvnd, lib32-mesa, lib32-llvm-libs,
#                         lib32-wayland and the rest), which is what 32-bit games through Proton need
# Vulkan for the Intel GPU (vulkan-intel, lib32-vulkan-intel) is in packages.desktop, for every machine.
linux-cachyos-nvidia-open nvidia-utils lib32-nvidia-utils libva-nvidia-driver
